  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0 (package.json), AGPL (composer.json).",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 34 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead.",
        "  AGPL-3.0 (package.json) is a deprecated SPDX id, replaced because it does not say whether -only or -or-later is meant.",
        "  No SPDX id: AGPL (composer.json). Only an SPDX id says which licence is meant, and for a GNU licence whether -only or -or-later.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node 16 stated in .nvmrc.",
        "  Not stated in engines.node in package.json, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (.eslintrc.cjs, superseded form), Stylelint (.stylelintrc.cjs), REUSE (.reuse/dep5), EditorConfig (.editorconfig).",
        " ESLint is configured in .eslintrc.cjs: ESLint 9 reads the flat config only; the eslintrc form, an .eslintrc file or the eslintConfig key in package.json, is ignored unless the run is pinned to ESLint 8.",
        " No Psalm configuration: the PHP side has no static analysis, which is what catches a wrong type before the server does.",
        " No PHPUnit configuration: there is no test harness in the checkout, so nothing can be run against a change.",
        " No PHP-CS-Fixer configuration: no coding standard is applied to the PHP sources, so formatting is settled in review instead of by a command."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "5 declared packages are named nowhere in the checkout: @babel/eslint-plugin, core-js, normalize.css, npm-check-updates, postcss-scss.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 50 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
